  "content": {
    "id": "p10-q27-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "27",
    "prompt": "Show that the sum of two consecutive triangular numbers is a perfect square.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$T_n+T_{n+1}=(n+1)^2$.\n\nSubstitute the triangular-number formulas and factorise.",
      "worked": "Using $T_n=\\dfrac{n(n+1)}{2}$,\n$$\\begin{align*}\nT_n+T_{n+1}&=\\frac{n(n+1)}{2}+\\frac{(n+1)(n+2)}{2}\\\\\nT_n+T_{n+1}&=\\frac{(n+1)(n+n+2)}{2}\\\\\nT_n+T_{n+1}&=\\frac{(n+1)(2n+2)}{2}\\\\\nT_n+T_{n+1}&=(n+1)^2.\n\\end{align*}$$\nSince $n+1$ is an integer, this is a perfect square.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 42
  },
